RangeForce: Active Information Gathering — Portfolio Write-Up
Platform: RangeForce
Room: Active Information Gathering
Difficulty: Intermediate
Date: 2026
Objective
Perform active reconnaissance against a target system to identify open ports, running services, exposed applications, and potential vulnerabilities using industry-standard security tools.
Step 1: Network Enumeration & Service Discovery
I began by conducting an aggressive network scan using Nmap (nmap -A) against the target host.
This scan enabled:
Open port identification
Service and version detection
Operating system fingerprinting
Default script enumeration
The results provided a comprehensive overview of the target’s attack surface and identified accessible services requiring further investigation.
Step 2: External Intelligence & Service Validation
After identifying exposed services, I used Shodan to gather additional intelligence regarding publicly indexed services and banner information related to the target.
This helped validate:
Service exposure
Potential known vulnerabilities
Publicly available metadata
This step expanded reconnaissance beyond direct scanning and added contextual awareness to the assessment.
Step 3: Application & Service Enumeration
With services identified, I performed deeper enumeration:
I used DirBuster to discover hidden directories and files within the web application.
I used FileZilla to test FTP connectivity and check for anonymous login access.
I used OWASP ZAP to conduct automated web application vulnerability scanning.
These tools allowed me to identify:
Hidden web directories
Misconfigured FTP permissions
Potential web application security weaknesses
Conclusion & Outcome
By combining active network scanning with application-level enumeration, I built a comprehensive profile of the target system’s attack surface.
This lab demonstrates core penetration testing skills:
Active reconnaissance
Service and version enumeration
Web application discovery
Vulnerability identification
The exercise reinforced the importance of structured information gathering before attempting exploitation.
